# Build output. Several GB, and Cargo.lock is what makes builds reproducible.
/target
Cargo.zip

# RUNTIME STATE, AND IT HOLDS SECRETS.
#
# servers.json is the local enrolment store, and an enrolled server's entry
# contains its key in plaintext - anyone holding one can post routing as that
# world. servers.cache.json is the last good platform response; it carries key
# HASHES rather than keys, but it is still another server's data and it is
# still state, not source.
#
# Both are written by the node next to the binary, which on Pelican is the
# server root. Neither belongs in a repository that a game host clones.
servers.json
servers.cache.json
*.cache.json

# Cargo home, when CARGO_HOME points at the working directory (the Pelican
# install script does this so the registry cache survives the container).
/.cargo

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
